# Only item_icons/ is ignored -- it's regenerated by tools/fetch_item_icons.py
# (run it after cloning), so committing it would just be redundant. Assets/ui/,
# Assets/map/, and Assets/maps/ are NOT ignored on purpose: those are your
# manually-captured screenshots/crops with no script to regenerate them, and
# the macro's image-search navigation (nav_start, victory, stage rows, map
# cards, ...) flatly doesn't work without them -- excluding them would ship
# a broken macro to anyone who clones the repo.
Assets/item_icons/
# Same reasoning -- regenerated by tools/fetch_stage_data.py.
Assets/stage_data.json

# Generated at runtime -- debug captures, recorded paths, saved templates,
# the task queue. None of it is meaningful to anyone but you.
debug/
Paths/*
Templates/*
# Record block input recordings (core/input_record.py) -- personal, no
# shipped-defaults exception like Paths/defaults/ below (there's no
# game-wide "known good" recording to ship; every one is bespoke).
Recordings/*

# Paths/defaults/ is the exception -- known-good walk paths for specific
# maps/acts (Fairy King Forest, King's Tomb, Spirit City Act 3) that the
# macro's Pre Start step looks up by name (see Assets/default_walk_paths.json
# and core.paths.load_path's fallback). Shared game data, not personal
# recordings, so unlike the rest of Paths/ it ships with the repo -- without
# it, the auto-walk feature would just silently do nothing for anyone who
# clones this.
!Paths/defaults/

# Templates/examples/ is the same exception for routines: ready-made macros
# that ship with the app so a new user has somewhere to start other than a
# blank editor (Macro Manager > Examples, see core.templates.list_examples).
# Shared game knowledge rather than anyone's personal setup, and deliberately
# a subfolder -- list_templates() uses os.listdir, so these never appear in
# the user's own Load... list and can never be saved over.
!Templates/examples/

# Personal config -- includes your Discord webhook URL, hotkeys, calibrated
# regions, etc. Never commit this.
settings.json

# Runtime log -- local troubleshooting only, no reason to version it.
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Build output -- see build_pyinstaller.py / build_bootstrap.py. The
# release workflow builds these fresh in CI; never commit a local build.
build/
dist/
*.spec
.bootstrap_version

# Personal Claude Code permission grants -- not team-wide.
.claude/settings.local.json
